<span style="font-size:11px">Dear,</span><br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:11px"><span style="line-height:20.8px">Thank you for your interest&nbsp;in graduate studies at the Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts School of Music at ASU. As one of the largest universities in the country, the ASU School of Music awards over $2 million to students annually, providing an excellent education at an unbeatable value. ASU&#39;s diverse and innovative community is a perfect complement to the personal attention you will receive in the School of Music. With a population of around 750 students, we offer small class sizes, state-of-the-art facilities and one-on-one instruction from world-renowned faculty. We invite you to consider the ASU School of Music for this important step in your music studies.</span></span>
<span style="line-height:20.7999992370605px"><img align="right" height="240" src="https://gallery.mailchimp.com/1d137137996f57d2118a53d3f/images/58469b69-177a-46b8-b21b-c91a19b500ec.jpg" style="width: 160px; height: 240px; margin: 0px;" width="160" /><br />
Dr. Kimberly Marshall</span><br style="line-height: 20.7999992370605px;" />
<span style="line-height:20.7999992370605px">Professor</span><br style="line-height: 20.7999992370605px;" />
<span style="line-height:20.7999992370605px">Organ</span><br style="line-height: 20.7999992370605px;" />
<a href="mailto:Kimberly.Marshall@asu.edu" style="line-height: 20.7999992370605px;" target="_blank">Kimberly.Marshall@asu.edu</a>
<span style="font-size:12px"><strong>The ASU Organ Studio</strong></span>

<p dir="ltr"><span style="font-size:11px">The ASU Organ Studio offers graduate students opportunities to increase understanding of the development of the organ and its music, while also allowing students to focus on their area of interest. Kimberly Marshall is an expert on medieval and Renaissance organ music.&nbsp;She specializes in Italian music, and the presence of the Italian baroque organ by Domenico Traeri (1742) and provides an ideal vehicle for exploring this style. Unlike other graduate programs in organ, where the main instruments are in multi-purpose halls that must be shared with chamber, choral and orchestral musicians, the Fritts and Traeri organs are located in a space dedicated to organ playing.&nbsp;Every student receives several hours of regularly scheduled practice times in the ASU Organ Hall each week in addition to lessons.&nbsp;Kimberly Marshall is committed to helping each of her graduate students find a unique voice in playing the organ, whether through church work, pedagogy, concert performances, multimedia collaborations or community relations. All of her graduate students obtain church jobs in the local area within the first year of their studies. Kimberly Marshall also coordinates studio trips to visit important organs in the US and abroad. Recent study tour locations include Mexico, France, the Netherlands, and Saxony. &nbsp;</span></p>
<span style="font-size:11px"> <strong>Degrees offered:</strong><br />
Master of Music: Performance<br />
Master of Music: Performance Pedagogy<br />
Doctor of Musical Arts: Performance<br />
<br />
For an idea of course requirements please view the <a href="http://music.asu.edu/students/grad/checksheets.php" target="_blank">checksheets</a>.</span>

