<span style="font-size:12px"><strong>Tuition | Financial Aid</strong></span><br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:11px">Current tuition and fees are reasonable and may be calculated with the <a href="https://students.asu.edu/tuition">ASU Tuition Estimator</a>.&nbsp;Music Scholarships and teaching assistantships are available. Typical assistantships are 25% which amount to 10 hours of work per week and receive:</span>

<ul>
	<li><span style="font-size:11px">Tuition remission covering the non-resident portion of tuition</span></li>
	<li><span style="font-size:11px">50% reduction in the resident portion of tuition (excluding fees)</span></li>
	<li><span style="font-size:11px">$7,450 stipend for the academic year, distributed over bi-weekly paychecks</span></li>
</ul>
<span style="font-size:11px"><strong>Spoken English Requirement: </strong>If your native language is not English you must meet spoken English requirements <em>before</em> you can be considered for a teaching assistantship. You may complete the <a href="https://aecp.asu.edu/international-teaching-assistants">ASU SPEAK test</a> (minimum score of 55) which is only available on the ASU campus or by attaining a 26 on the speaking portion of the TOEFL. For full details, please visit this <a href="http://music.asu.edu/admissions/grad/assistantships.php">website</a>.</span>

<span style="font-size:12px"><strong>Application Process</strong></span><br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:11px"><strong><span style="color:rgb(153, 0, 51)">Step 1:</span></strong> Apply to <a href="https://students.asu.edu/graduate/apply">ASU Graduate Admissions</a> and prepare the following:</span>

<ul>
	<li><span style="font-size:11px">Official Transcripts: Sealed hardcopy transcripts from all undergraduate and graduate coursework&nbsp;</span></li>
	<li><span style="font-size:11px"><a href="https://students.asu.edu/graduate/proficiency">English Proficiency</a>: Applicants from a country whose native language is not English will be required to show proof of English Proficiency by the application deadline</span></li>
</ul>
<span style="font-size:11px"> <span style="color:rgb(153, 0, 51)"><strong>Step 2:</strong></span> Submit the School of Music Application</span>

<ul>
	<li style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size:11px">Contact information for 3 - 4 references</span></li>
	<li style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size:11px">Resume</span></li>
	<li style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size:11px">Personal Statement</span></li>
	<li style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size:11px">Repertoire List</span></li>
	<li style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size:11px"><a href="http://music.asu.edu/admissions/auditions/prescreening.php#dma">Prescreening</a> (doctoral applicants only)</span></li>
	<li style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size:11px">Teaching Assistantship Application (optional)</span></li>
</ul>

<div style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size:11px"><strong><span style="color:rgb(153, 0, 51)">Step 3</span>: </strong>Audition</span></div>

<ul>
	<li style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size:11px">Complete an ad-hoc audition (doctoral or master&#39;s) or a&nbsp;<a href="http://music.asu.edu/admissions/auditions/#recorded">recorded audition</a>&nbsp;<span style="line-height:20.8px">(master&#39;s applicants only)</span></span></li>
	<li style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size:11px">Applicants should contact Dr. Marshall&nbsp;to arrange an ad-hoc audition date and time.&nbsp;<span style="line-height:20.8px">All School of Music materials must be received at least one week prior to&nbsp;the ad-hoc audition date.</span></span></li>
</ul>

